q:
An application emits this JSON log and sets no other severity field:

{"level": "WARN", "msg": "disk 85% full"}

With the default preprocessing configuration, what status does the log get?

A syslog-style line ends with an embedded JSON payload:

Sep 06 09:13:38 vagrant program[123]: server.1 {"method":"GET", "status_code":200}

The line as a whole is not JSON, so it is not parsed automatically. Which Grok element, placed at the end of the rule, turns the trailing JSON into attributes such as `method` and `status_code`?
